WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.435
-That's all the time we have
for life coach.

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.371
My thanks to the great
Jerry Seinfeld.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:06.639
Stick around. We'll be talking
with Jerry after the break.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.074 line:0%
Come on back, everybody.

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:10.810 line:0%
I know you love baseball.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.013
How are you feeling
about the return of baseball?

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.714
Are you eager
to get back to a stadium?

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.651
-Very much. Very much.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.853
I don't know why
people always think

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:24.657
that I should be involved
in ownership in baseball.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.325
Like, "Why don't you --"
you know?

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.228
And I always try
and explain to people

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:32.798
the absolute pinnacle
of being a fan of baseball

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:36.669
is a hot dog, a beer,
and a seat.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.605
That is the top
of Mount Olympus.

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.341
Everything that you think
will make it better doesn't.

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:44.544
-Yeah, you're absolutely right.
-It doesn't.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.980
Yeah, you're at the top
of Mount Olympus.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.449
-Do you like the social aspect
of going to a game,

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:53.019
or do you want to just focus
on the game?

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.953
-I really like
to focus on the game.

00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:57.357
I'm very interested in
what's going on every second.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:00.659
I find it
a very complicated game.

00:01:00.659 --> 00:01:06.366
And, you know, every pitch
changes every situation.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.202
But there is always
the socializing,

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:13.306
and, you know,
people like to go.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:18.544
And, yeah, but, you know,
I like eating and watching

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:19.946
and not talking too much.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.815
I really like to eat a lot.

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:25.819
-Yeah.
-I once did a --

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.754
one of the early games I went to
after I moved back to New York

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:31.290
in the 2000s,

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.960
and they shot me at a game

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.330
and then put together
all the food I ate.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.567
It was kind of embarrassing.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.702
-That's kind of good.
I like that.

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:44.937
I never know what to do --

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.506
-I always have a thing
with Matthew Broderick.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:49.709
Anytime Matthew goes to a game
or I go to a game,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.578
if we don't go together,
which we do a lot,

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.279
but if we don't go together,

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.482
we always text a list
of everything that was consumed,

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.618
every item of food.

